<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n39359" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">-ptĕ</span></b> , a pronominal suffix appended to
			adjective and (more rarely) to substantive personal
		pronouns, esp. in the ablative; the Engl. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>self</i>, <i>own</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">meopte ingenio,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Ps. 3, 2, 14</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>1.</b> With <i>adj. pron.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">meāpte malitiā,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Truc. 2, 5, 18</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tuopte ingenio,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Capt. 2, 3, 11</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Tac. H. 2, 63</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">suopte pondere,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					N. D. 1, 25, 69</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">suāpte manu,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					de Or. 3, 3, 10</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nostrāpte culpā,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ter.
					Phorm. 5, 2, 1</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> With
				<i>subst. pron.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mepte fieri servum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Men. 5, 8, 10</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">suumpte amicum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Mil. 2, 4, 38</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
